Package: hallfast
Type: Package
Title: Fast Solver for the Hall Adult Body Weight Model
Version: 0.1.0
Date: 2026-10-15
Authors@R:
    person("Chris", "Kypridemos", email = "c.kypridemos@liverpool.ac.uk",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Converts changes in energy intake into changes in body weight
    and body mass index (BMI) using the dynamic adult body weight model of
    Hall et al. (2011) <doi:10.1016/S0140-6736(11)60812-X>, as specified in
    its web appendix. Instead of integrating the model day by day, the solver
    uses exact closed-form solutions for adaptive thermogenesis,
    extracellular fluid and glycogen, reduces fat and lean mass to a single
    equation through Forbes partitioning, and integrates it with an adaptive
    Dormand-Prince 5(4) method. Annual results are obtained several hundred
    times faster than with daily time-stepping, with errors below 0.001 kg.
    Optional proportional appetite feedback follows Hall (2024)
    <doi:10.1002/oby.24027>, a compatibility mode reproduces the 'bw'
    package, and a slow high-precision reference solver is included for
    validation. Designed for large microsimulation models.
